From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TeeJayBaker <Tom_John_baker@yahoo.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:46:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Launcher: a Frame rate choice for games shown at every
 display tick (present_interval display)

A profile with present_interval display and no fps_target runs at 60 fps by showing a frame at
every display tick where the game asks for two (Monster Train 2, Overcooked! All You Can Eat).
Their players had no 30 fps choice in the launcher: only DM_PRESENT_INTERVAL=game in an env file,
while every fps_target game offers Frame rate 30 / 60. 30 is the Switch's rate and uses less
power (Overcooked on an M1 Pro: about 0.15 W of CPU at 30 fps, 0.86 W at 60).

settings.tsv: a Frame rate row for DM_PRESENT_INTERVAL (game = 30 fps, display = 60 fps, default
display), shown for DM_GAME_PRESENT_DISPLAY==1&DM_GAME_FPS_TARGET==0, so a game with both keys
keeps its one DM_FPS_TARGET row. settings.py: a condition of several joined by & holds when all do.

Tests: test_launcher_settings.py (Monster Train 2 and Overcooked get the row; Monster Hunter Rise,
display with fps_target, keeps only DM_FPS_TARGET; Super Mario Bros. Wonder gets neither),
test_settings.py, test_docs.py. Not run in a front end.

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#836
Reason: Monster Train 2 and Overcooked run at 60 fps with no 30 fps choice in the launcher
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#369

